course: dictionary
lesson: 13839
title: Words that show feelings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how a person feels and how they want others to feel. Read this: «The crowd gave a jeering laugh when the player missed the goal.» The word jeering is the clue. A crowd with a jeering laugh is not cheering the player on. It is laughing at him to make him feel small.
explain: Use the words around the new word to check your idea. The player missed the goal, and the laugh is the crowd's reaction. Ask: what word would fit here? Try cheering in the sentence: «The crowd gave a cheering laugh.» That does not fit a missed goal in the same way, so jeering must mean mocking.
explain: Jeering can work as a verb, an adjective or a noun. «They were jeering at the noisy boy.» «A jeering voice shouted from the back.» «Jeering hurts people.» Each time it still means mocking someone in a rude way.
fact: Jeering means shouting or laughing at someone in a rude, mocking way.
fact: «Jeering crowd» means a crowd that mocks someone.
fact: «A jeering laugh» is a laugh that makes fun of someone.
fact: Jeering is unkind, so it is the opposite of cheering, which shows support.
fact: Jeer is the base word, and jeering is its -ing form.
exercise: «The crowd began jeering when the team lost the match.» What is the crowd doing? | Sleeping quietly in their seats | Singing a happy song | Cheering the team on | *Mocking the team in a rude way
exercise: «She ignored the jeering voices and kept on walking.» What were the voices doing? | Giving her a present | Whispering a secret | *Mocking her in a rude way | Asking her for directions
exercise: Choose the best meaning of «a jeering laugh». | A very quiet laugh | A kind, gentle laugh | *A rude laugh that makes fun of someone | A laugh that tickles
test: Mia says jeering is the same as cheering. Why is she wrong? | Cheering is rude and jeering is kind | They mean exactly the same thing | *Cheering shows support, but jeering is unkind and mocking | Jeering means singing a happy song
test: «The jeering kids stopped when the teacher walked in.» What does jeering mean here? | Helping a friend with homework | *Mocking someone in a rude way | Waving at the teacher | Singing quietly
exam: Which sentence shows that jeering is unkind? | *«Jeering at a friend hurts their feelings.» | «Jeering helps the team win the match.» | «Jeering is the same as saying thank you.» | «Jeering makes everyone feel happy.»
